From: JorreFog <JorreFog@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] core_info: the system image's cores listed besides libretro_directory's

On BananaOS the cores that come with the system are in /usr/lib/libretro, on
a read-only image, so the Core Downloader can only install into a folder on
the card (libretro_directory). RetroArch lists the cores of one folder; the
image's folder is listed too, so Load Core, the core information and the
running core's details keep the image's cores while downloaded ones are added.
A folder that doesn't exist yet (no download so far) isn't an error when the
image's folder is there.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [BananaOS-specific]
---
--- a/core_info.c
+++ b/core_info.c
@@ -23,6 +23,11 @@
 #include <streams/interface_stream.h>
 #include <formats/rjson.h>
 #include <lists/dir_list.h>
+
+/* BananaOS: the system image's own cores (read-only), listed besides libretro_directory's */
+#if defined(__linux__) && !defined(BANANA_IMAGE_CORE_DIR)
+#define BANANA_IMAGE_CORE_DIR "/usr/lib/libretro"
+#endif
 #include <file/archive_file.h>
 
 #ifdef HAVE_CONFIG_H
@@ -1424,6 +1429,15 @@
       }
    }
 #else
+#if defined(__linux__) && defined(BANANA_IMAGE_CORE_DIR)
+   /* BananaOS: the cores that come with the system image are listed too,
+    * besides the ones the Core Downloader put in libretro_directory (on the
+    * card: the image is read-only) */
+   if (!string_is_equal(core_dir, BANANA_IMAGE_CORE_DIR))
+      dir_list_ok = dir_list_append(path_list->dir_list,
+            BANANA_IMAGE_CORE_DIR, exts, false, show_hidden_files,
+            false, false) || dir_list_ok;
+#endif
    /* Keep the old 'directory not found' behaviour */
    if (!dir_list_ok)
       goto error;
